From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nickEatsBread <nickEatsBread@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:49:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] streaming: take a piece a stream is about to read off a
 slow peer sooner

librqbit gives each piece to a single peer and lets another peer take it over only after ten
times the thief's average piece time. A player blocked on that piece stalls for the whole wait
while the rest of the swarm keeps delivering other pieces.

The first eight pieces ahead of every open stream are now critical. Before a peer starts
anything else, it takes over a critical piece that another peer has held for 1.5 times this
peer's average piece time, never sooner than 500 ms. A peer that has not completed a piece has
no average and takes nothing.

A peer that takes a piece over requests only the chunks still missing. Re-requesting every chunk
in order put the missing ones last.
